 to individuals, families, and business owners through individual, independent corporate, and affiliated corporate agencies; banks; independent associates/career agents; and brokers. Aflac Incorporated was founded in 1955 and is headquartered in Columbus, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel Paul Amos | Chairman & CEO | Age 73 | Compensation: $9.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["AFLAC Incorporated is a large-cap financial services business with a $61.5B market cap on $17.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 8% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 22\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 7.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 54% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5363305842939368},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $44.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["41 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Aflac Incorporated $AFL Stock: Private Wealth Asset Management LLC Raises Holdings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/aflac-incorporated-afl-stock-private-wealth-asset-management-llc-raises-holdings.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795174495.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.977,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"How Did Aflac (NYSE:AFL) Extend Its Long Streak of Dividend Increases?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stoc